  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "عَلِيٌّ عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عِيسَى عَنْ يُونُسَ عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مُسْكَانَ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ قَالَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "ʿAlī, from Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā, from Yūnus, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Miskān, from Abī ʿAbd Allāh عليه السلام, who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "إِذَا قَتَلَتِ الْمَرْأَةُ رَجُلًا قُتِلَتْ بِهِ، وَإِذَا قَتَلَ الرَّجُلُ الْمَرْأَةَ فَإِنْ أَرَادُوا الْقَوَدَ أَدَّوْا فَضْلَ دِيَةِ الرَّجُلِ وَأَقَادُوهُ بِهَا، وَإِنْ لَمْ يَفْعَلُوا قَبِلُوا الدِّيَةَ دِيَةَ الْمَرْأَةِ كَامِلَةً، وَدِيَةُ الْمَرْأَةِ نِصْفُ دِيَةِ الرَّجُلِ."
      "translations": {
        "en": "If a woman kills a man, she is killed for him. And if a man kills a woman, then if they desire retaliation, they must pay the excess of the man’s blood-money, and then retaliate against him for her. But if they do not do that, they accept the blood-money—the full blood-money of the woman—and the blood-money of the woman is half the blood-money of the man."
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith states a legal ruling concerning retaliation and blood-money between men and women in cases of homicide. It explains that qisas applies differently depending on whether the victim is male or female, and specifies that the diyah of a woman is half the diyah of a man.",
      "seo_question": "What is the ruling on qisas and diyah when a man kills a woman or a woman kills a man in Shia fiqh?",
      "key_terms": {
        "الْمَرْأَةُ": "the woman; the female party in the homicide ruling",
        "رَجُلًا": "a man; the male victim mentioned in the ruling",
        "الْقَوَدَ": "retaliatory execution; legal retaliation in homicide",
        "دِيَةِ": "blood-money; financial compensation due in a homicide case",
        "فَضْلَ": "the excess amount; the difference that must be paid",
        "كَامِلَةً": "in full; complete payment without reduction within the stated ruling"
      }
    }
  },
